# Jekyll Academic Website - Project Overview

This is a Jekyll-based academic website using the al-folio theme. The site supports both English and Chinese content with a focus on software engineering, design patterns, and technical tutorials.

## Key Configuration Files
- [config.yml](mdc:_config.yml) - Main Jekyll configuration with site settings, plugins, and theme options
- [Gemfile](mdc:Gemfile) - Ruby dependencies and Jekyll plugins
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Node.js dependencies for development tools

## Content Structure
- `_posts/` - Main blog posts (English)
- `_i18n/zh/_posts/` - Chinese blog posts
- `_pages/` - Static pages (about, projects, publications, etc.)
- `_projects/` - Project showcase pages
- `_books/` - Book reviews and summaries
- `_news/` - News and announcements

## Layouts and Templates
- `_layouts/` - Page templates (post, page, about, cv, etc.)
- `_includes/` - Reusable components (header, footer, social links, etc.)
- `_sass/` - SCSS stylesheets and theme customization

## Key Features
- Multi-language support (English/Chinese)
- Academic publications with citations
- Project portfolio
- Blog with categories and tags
- SEO optimization
- Google Analytics integration
- Comments system (Giscus)
- Responsive design

## Development Workflow
- Posts use YAML front matter for metadata
- Images stored in `assets/img/`
- CSS/JS in `assets/css/` and `assets/js/`
- Custom plugins in `_plugins/`
